{"qid":"Q267816","names":["Duchy of Benevento"],"title":"Duchy of Benevento","endonym":null,"capsule":"The Duchy of Benevento was a Lombard duchy in southern Italy, founded by Zotto around 571 and consolidated by his nephew Arechis I; its geographic separation from the northern Lombard kingdom by the Papal States gave it de facto autonomy throughout the seventh and eighth centuries. Duke Grimoald I used it as a base to seize the Lombard kingship in 662, while later dukes resisted Carolingian authority with varying success. After Charlemagne dissolved the Lombard kingdom in 774, Arechis II proclaimed himself Prince of Benevento, transforming the entity into the Principality of Benevento. The Norman adventurer Robert Guiscard finally conquered the last remnants of the Lombard south by 1078, and the broader region was organised into the County of Apulia, absorbed definitively into the Norman Kingdom of Sicily by 1130.","attestation":"Boundaries from Seshat Cliopatria (Bennett et al., Scientific Data 2025; CC BY 4.0), digitized from standard historical atlases at ~0.07° resolution. The duchy's political existence is well-documented in Lombard and Carolingian sources; its frontier with Byzantine-held Calabria and the papal corridor was fluid and is mapped at best approximately.","attestationLinks":[{"label":"Cliopatria dataset (Seshat, CC BY 4.0)","url":"https://github.com/Seshat-Global-History-Databank/cliopatria"},{"label":"Bennett et al. 2025, Scientific Data","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41597-025-04516-9"}],"citations":[{"label":"Wikipedia: Duchy of Benevento","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Duchy_of_Benevento"},{"label":"Britannica: Benevento","url":"https://www.britannica.com/place/Benevento-duchy-Italy"},{"label":"Wikipedia: Lombards","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lombards"}],"britannica":null,"cowCode":null,"wikipedia":"Duchy of Benevento","rulers":[{"qid":null,"name":"Zotto","nativeName":"Zotto","roman":"Zotto","start":571,"end":591,"imag